WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.060
Good morning John. Last night, as we must
do in this day and age, I was Googling. I

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.270
don't even remember what I was searching for
but as you (I'm sure) know, Google nowadays

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:11.730
actually attempts to guess what you want to
know before you finish telling it what you

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.800
want to know. Because apparently we're so
lazy that we'd rather not move our fingers

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.770
any more than necessary. It's a clever little
trick and I imagine that it works basically

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.609
by figuring out what other people have searched
for that start with the same letters as what

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:27.900
you are searching for. Which is I guess, convenient-ish.
But more than the value is convenient, I think

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.009
the real value is it's ability to uh, help
us peer into the soul of mankind.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:35.800
So let's say we start out with “is”. Lots
of Google queries must begin with the letters

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.440
“I S” and then space. And here we have
“is Facebook down?” which is probably

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.680
something people search a lot when Facebook
goes down. But the second most common question

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.750
starting with “is” asked to Google is
“is lady gaga a man?”. I'll just go ahead

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.860
and answer that one for everyone. No. No,
Lady Gaga is not a man.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.989
And then we have the beginning of a trend
that we will see a lot in Google auto-complete,

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:59.079
“Is Daniel Tosh gay?", "Is Justin Bieber
gay?", Is Nate Berkus gay?” I don't even

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:00.410
know who Nate Berkus is!

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.640
But to peer deeper into our nation's psyche,
you can type “Is my” and find out what

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.569
people are curious about concerning their
possessions. Including, “Is my husband gay?",

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:13.369
"Is my boyfriend gay?", "Is my mac 64 bit”
which is actually a legitimate normal Google

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:17.840
question why aren't they all like that. “Is
my license suspended?” - which is a question

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.549
you should really know the answer to and “Is
my house haunted?”. Which... I am amazed.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:29.709
I, I am, I am just amazed. And then go deeper,
just type a random letter, “is my d-", "Is

00:01:29.709 --> 00:01:35.490
my dog pregnant?", "Is my dog sick?", "Is
my dog dying?", "Is my dog gay?” Yes, your

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.899
dog is– yeah actually your dog is probably
bisexu– actually your dog is probably omni-sexual.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:43.670
Your dog has probably had sex with pillows,
your dog is probably ejaculating on the arm

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.770
of a couch right now. Wow, our hangups. We
have them.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.899
And then I had a bit of inspiration, and I
had to go ahead and type in, “Is John Green-”

00:01:50.899 --> 00:01:54.409
and John, I know you want to know what the
world wants to know about you. “Is John

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:59.130
Green married?”. Yes. “Is John Green gay?".
Is John Green gay? Why does everybody want

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.169
to know if everybody's gay?

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:05.119
Let me just go ahead and answer all of these
questions for you. We have yes, no, yes, yes,

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:09.119
no. John Green is not dead. So of course now
that I know what people want to know about

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:13.760
you, I had to figure out what people want
to know about me. And... Piece of a rooster

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.300
fard knock a mother of poo. No one cares about
what Hank Green is. So let me ask you guys

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.319
a favor, could you go uh, Google “Is Hank
Green awesome?”. Maybe if enough people

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:25.439
do it, it will auto-complete. I find this
exploration fascinating, particularly our

00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:28.879
obsession with the sexual orientation of other
people. And I am looking forward to delving

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:32.440
deeper into our nations psyche using the tool
of Google Auto-complete.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.329
And of course finally, I had to ask Google
what people are asking about Google. One letter

00:02:36.329 --> 00:02:39.569
into it we're already asking if Google is
making us stupid, but we're also asking “Is

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:43.510
god real?” and “Is gonorrhea curable?”.
But go ahead and type in “is Google ga-”

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.930
and you will find out that fewer people are
asking if Google is gaining a monopoly on

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.189
the world’s information, than are asking
whether Google is gay. John, Google is a genderless

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:55.700
website that hopefully, has never had a thought.
Much less a feeling of romantic longing. And

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.519
thus we can all assume that Google... is not
gay.

00:02:58.519 --> 00:02:59.780
John, I will see you on Monday.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.730
Some various news, I just did a collab for
you with HorribleFiction and you can click

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.840
to watch it here. The winners for the Project
For Awesome Raffle have been announced and

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.290
you have been contacted if you won. If you
haven't been contacted, you win at giving

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.849
money to charity. Thank you. I hope you all
have a very, very, very, very, very, very,

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:16.900
very, very, very Happy New Year.

